r every day."]', '["Your gold is solid. Why is your color painted on?", "Hand sanitizer, lotion, keyboard: the blue stays blue.", "You''ve saved this ring six times. Here''s what''s stopping you.", "Color that''s part of the material, not a coat on top.", "The first colored ring you won''t take off to wash your hands."]', '["Side-by-side macro: a coated colored ring after months of wear vs a Venzi ceramic band, with text naming the scratch- and chemical-resistance claim (no drop tests).", "A ''day in the hands'' POV: sanitizer, dishes, typing, gym bag. The Geo ring never comes off, captioned with the no-special-handling claim.", "Stacking demo: her existing plain gold bands with one Geo or Hex ring added, showing color as an addition, not a replacement."]', '[{"slug": "built-in-not-painted-on", "pillar": "education", "description": "Explains ceramic inlay vs coated or painted color, so she sees color as durable, not delicate."}, {"slug": "sanitizer-test", "pillar": "mechanism", "description": "Shows the scratch- and chemical-resistant ceramic through a normal workday, ending on the $2,000 Geo ring."}, {"slug": "one-color-in-the-stack", "pillar": "emotion", "description": "The relief of finally wearing the colored ring she''s been saving, next to the gold she already owns."}]', true, 6, ts, ts),
